## 11. Required tests

Add or repair automated tests for all of the following.

### Monitoring tests

- Every available M action is read-only.
- Source-unavailable, empty, stale, partial, invalid, and error states remain distinguishable.
- Missing values never become zero or healthy.
- Search, filters, sorting, selection, detail drawers, and navigation work.
- Home-to-detail values and filters reconcile to the same authoritative dataset.
- Trends require multiple compatible timestamped observations.
- No unsupported field or native SAP identifier is fabricated.

### Warning tests

- A rule without required source data or an approved policy is not evaluated.
- A valid finding includes rule identity and traceable evidence.
- “No findings” is distinguishable from “not evaluated.”
- Missing, stale, or invalid data cannot generate a false healthy state.
- Duplicate findings follow an explicit deduplication rule.
- Lifecycle operations work only on supported warning records and persist only if persistence is implemented.
- Warning actions never invoke SAP or OS mutations.

### Execution safety tests

- All state-changing E actions are disabled in Phase 1.
- Direct invocation or dispatch of an E action is denied.
- No execution handler calls an external write endpoint or OS/database command.
- No fake success or completed-operation state is emitted.
- Missing authorization, adapter, policy, or preflight gates cannot be bypassed.
- Read-only M actions continue to work.

### Whole-application tests

- All ten island routes load.
- Fixed navigation order and approved Home composition remain intact.
- M/W/E controls and reasons are localized in English and Persian.
- RTL/LTR switching preserves route, filters, and selected record.
- Desktop, tablet, and mobile layouts remain usable without unintended horizontal overflow.
- No placeholder control is represented as a working capability.
- No conflicting source or KPI formula is introduced across pages.

Update `tests/ACCEPTANCE_CHECKLIST.md` and add an explicit M/W/E acceptance matrix. Never mark tests PASS unless they were actually run.

